// PENDING: from an OPEN SigmaHQ pull request. Not reviewed or merged by SigmaHQ yet.
// Pull request: #6030 new: OpenAI Codex sandbox abuse detection rules
// Pull request URL: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/pull/6030
// Pull request author: swachchhanda000
// Change: new rule
// Title: OpenAI Codex Sandbox Configuration Files Modified By Unexpected Process
// Sigma ID: a2c6d4e7-1f3b-4a8c-be1f-4b5c6d7e8f9a
// Status: experimental | Level: medium
// Author: Jonathan Johnson, Swachchhanda Shrawan Poudel (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2026-05-26 | Modified: -
// ATT&CK: credential-access, execution, persistence, stealth, T1552.001, T1574
// Description: Detects modification of sensitive OpenAI Codex sandbox configuration files under the .codex
//   directory by a process other than the legitimate Codex binaries. The .codex directory contains
//   the sandbox setup marker, encrypted sandbox user credentials (.sandbox-
//   secrets\sandbox_users.json), capability SIDs (cap_sid), and the command runner binary itself.
//   Tampering with these files by an unrelated process may indicate credential harvesting of the
//   DPAPI-encrypted sandbox credentials, persistence via replacement, or attempts to manipulate the
//   capability SID file to weaken workspace isolation. Note: Codex does not remove these artifacts
//   on uninstall, so they may be present on systems where Codex has been previously installed.
// False positives:
//   - Backup software that creates temporary copies of files for backup purposes following similar file directory patterns
// References:
//   - https://jonny-johnson.medium.com/a-deep-dive-into-codex-windows-sandbox-a2489bf4ae91
//   - https://openai.com/index/building-codex-windows-sandbox/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/a20c16d6d3eef0c2c625df9d2ac3e18c1b12187c/rules/windows/file/file_event/file_event_win_codex_config_dir_tampering.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language, Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceFileEvents
| where (FolderPath contains "\\.codex\\" and (FolderPath endswith "\\sandbox_users.json" or FolderPath endswith "\\setup_marker.json" or FolderPath endswith "\\cap_sid" or FolderPath endswith "\\sandbox.log")) and (not(((InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\codex.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\codex-windows-sandbox-setup.exe") and InitiatingProcessFolderPath contains "\\codex-command-runner-")))
